The fixture of the shell package's linked checks (ShellTest/Linked/Shell.lean,
shellChecks), which the linked test reads under the package's directory,
where it runs. It was the core's tests/shell, handed to contract-test, until
the shell moved out of the core. It must stay executable (mode 100755).

- hello: prints `hello` and a line feed, and exits 0. The linked test runs
  it with `shell-command` over the real process service, in this
  directory, and expects the echo area to say `hello`. Shell builtins only.
